- Deopt/resid stream split from prior round continues to be critical: makes true bailout prioritization obvious.

Lessons
- For expression mode APPs, structural residualization is generally the right default: build dynamic APP nodes directly and avoid whole-node ALO fallback unless net-level interaction constraints truly require it.
- Isolating true deopts shows the next fundamental work is cap/remodeling (arg/env) rather than additional APP micro-fixes.

Next likely steps
- Attack `HEAD_APP_ARG_CAP` as top blocker (likely redesign of argument handling rather than further cap bumps).
- Triage highest `EXPR_UNSUPPORTED_TAG` sites from admission benches, prioritizing tags/sites with largest hit counts.
- Keep strict local force REF policy conservative until mismatch continuation semantics are explicitly specified.
